# LangGraph Agent Patterns

## State Management

- Define state with `TypedDict` using `Annotated` reducers: `Annotated[list, add_messages]`
- Keep state under 50KB per checkpoint; store large data in external Store
- Use accumulators for growing data: messages, findings, errors

## Persistence

- Always use durable checkpointer: `PostgresSaver` or `SqliteSaver` — never `InMemorySaver` in prod
- Use `AsyncPostgresSaver.from_conn_string()` for async apps
- Set checkpoint TTL to prevent unbounded growth

## Human-in-the-Loop

- Use `interrupt()` for irreversible actions; resume with `Command`
- Route business-rule errors to `interrupt()` not retry
- Test resume across process restarts

## Failure Handling

- Design failure through graph topology (validation nodes, escalation edges)
- Classify: transient (retry), business-rule (escalate), LLM errors (bounded repair)
- Set recursion limit deliberately

## ReAct Pattern

- Use `create_agent` from `langchain.agents` — not deprecated `create_react_agent` from `langgraph.prebuilt`
- Import: `from langchain.agents import create_agent`
- Use `system_prompt` parameter for static prompts; use middleware for dynamic prompts
- Define tools with `@tool` decorator; docstring is selection criteria
- Include in docstring: what, when, params, return format, examples
- Keep tools atomic; complex = multiple composable tools
- Set iteration limits (5-10)
- Enable streaming
- Use persistent checkpointer
- Generate structured outputs only at final step

## Reflexion Pattern

- Three components: Actor, Evaluator, Reflector
- Loop: attempt -> evaluate -> critique -> store -> retry
- Use for complex reasoning where accuracy > latency
- Use LangGraph for orchestration
- Use Pydantic for structured outputs
- Watch for "degeneration-of-thought"
